      "writtenOn": "2024-02-19T07:32:18Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, the assumption is valid. The assumption is caused by guest DT, not only by host DT. I\u0027m not sure the detailed reason why you mentioned in non-pVM, but verification for non-pVM is executed like below.\n\n- Virtmgr extract vendor hashtree digest.\n- Virtmgr onstruct DTBO based on extracted value.\n- VIrtmgr passes DTBO to crosvm.\n- Crosvm uses DTBO to construct guest VM DT.\n- In first-stage init, guest VM searches vendor hashtree digest in its DT to enable dm-verity.\n\nCurrently I think it\u0027s due to lack of fstab \u0026 devicetree support on CF, but I\u0027m not 100% confident on it. Would I file a bug and make this as an TODO item?",
      "parentUuid": "7e6acc77_4fe7f81d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2131,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2133,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "5a62ce729ed6dd2a4aff5b2788ebef8bab3d4114",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "107622fb_00668810",
        "filename": "tests/testapk/src/java/com/android/microdroid/test/MicrodroidTests.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 2133,
      "author": {
        "id": 1019013
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-20T01:31:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "As you mentioned above, for botting non-pVM, content of the host DT isn\u0027t necessary for booting vendor partition. virtmgr will fill necessary vendor hashtree digest.\n\nCould you explain me bit more detail about \u0027assumption is caused by guest DT\u0027? What\u0027s special for running microdroid with vendor partition?",
      "parentUuid": "86dbb4a5_7f83fb16",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2131,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2133,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "5a62ce729ed6dd2a4aff5b2788ebef8bab3d4114",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b3019dbc_147cf465",
        "filename": "tests/testapk/src/java/com/android/microdroid/test/MicrodroidTests.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 2133,
      "author": {
        "id": 1950816
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-02-20T02:27:10Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e In first-stage init, guest VM searches vendor hashtree digest in its DT to enable dm-verity.\n\nHere\u0027s the exact answer. First fstab.microdroid leaves information where to read hashtree digest in init stage of VM. https://cs.android.com/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:packages/modules/Virtualization/microdroid/fstab.microdroid;l\u003d5\n\nBased on fstab.microdroid, first-stage init tries to read hashtree digest written as `/proc/device-tree/avf/vendor_hashtree_descriptor_root_digest`.\n\nBut in Cuttlefish, we don\u0027t have directory `/proc/device-tree`. So we cannot read hashtree digest from there. I haven\u0027t investigated about this in detail, but there\u0027s no `/proc/device-tree` in host \u0026 guest both.\n\nBTW, there\u0027s already a bug mentioning about this issue: b/325094712.",
      "parentUuid": "107622fb_00668810",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2131,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2133,
        "endChar": 0
      },
      "revId": "5a62ce729ed6dd2a4aff5b2788ebef8bab3d4114",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
